      "message": "#define CONFIG_WP_STORAGE_OFF CONFIG_EC_PROTECTED_STORAGE_OFF\n#define CONFIG_WP_STORAGE_SIZE CONFIG_EC_PROTECTED_STORAGE_SIZE\n\n#define _BINMAN_RO_PATH DT_PATH(binman, wp_ro)\n#define _BINMAN_RW_PATH DT_PATH(binman, ec_rw)\n\n#define CONFIG_EC_PROTECTED_STORAGE_OFF DT_PROP(_BINMAN_RO_PATH, offset)\n#define CONFIG_EC_PROTECTED_STORAGE_SIZE DT_PROP(_BINMAN_RO_PATH, size)\n\nwhen we lock RO part, we use CONFIG_WP_STORAGE_OFF and CONFIG_WP_STORAGE_SIZE to determine the lock range, so I am thinking: \n`CROS_EC_RO_SIZE` means ec code size.\n`CONFIG_EC_PROTECTED_STORAGE_SIZE` means the RO size, not only code but also other data we want to store and lock.\n\nIf I am getting those define right, then the /binman/wp-ro,size should be half of flash (assume we agree RO/RW took half of flash each).",
